en up the paper you  should have an X and a horizontal line  so now what we're going to do is we're  going to position this line in the  middle so that it is vertical and we're  going to take both of the top corners  and we're going to fold it inwards onto  that vertical line so that the top edge  here is on the vertical line so just  take the corner fold it inwards onto  that vertical line just like that and  make a crease do the same with the other  top edge  so you should have something that looks  just like this now what we're going to  do is we're going to fold the paper in  half like this  and now you have this other corner of  the paper and what you're going to do is  if you remember the waterbomb base we're  going to basically tuck this this corner  in just like that  so just take the other end here the edge  and you're going to tuck it in words to  the bottom just like that and now you  have these two flaps on the right side  tuck it in and then make the crease so  that's basically how you make each of  the modular units it's very simple so  I'm going to do it real quick with the  blue one now same thing fold it to  corner  opposite corner to opposite corner same  thing  fold one edge to the opposite edge  then open it up hold that center line  here vertically and then just fold the  top corners into that line  just like that then fold the model in  half like this  and then you're going to tuck this other  corner on the right side in towards the  center tuck it all the way in and then  close these two flaps that you now have  and make a crease and that's how you  make the modular unit so you should be  able to make the remaining six so what I  do with the post-it note is I peel it  off and I've marked where it's sticky  and you're going to hold that sticky  edge on the back then you're going to do  the two diagonal folds just like that  and now when you're going to make the  edge to edge fold I like to cut this  sticky edge in half by holding it  vertically on the back like this then  you fold the top edge down to the bottom  edge and I'll show you why I do that  it's because once you have made this  fold and you're going to fold the edges  in you're going to fold them in on the  sticky edge so that the two top corners  get stuck to the paper just like that  you see fold the corners in  fold it in half and now the same thing  just tuck this corner in here  and there you go interlocking the first  seven units is pretty much the same  exact thing it's really not that  difficult it's the last piece that might  be a little tricky so I'll focus mainly  on how to connect the last piece what  you're going to want to do is to first  set them up if you're using alternating  colors you're going to want to take two  different color units and you're going  to basically hold them like we just  finished creating them so you want these  two flaps on the right and you want the  two corners which you fold it in to be  on the left side just like this hold the  piece on the right the same exact way  then you'll see we have these edges here  right you want to have these two flaps  open and you're going to take this edge  here and you're going to twist it so  that it is completely vertical and then  you're going to slide the piece on the  right into the piece on the left until  this corner here is basically right in  between the top of those flaps right  there and you want to make sure that  this edge is all the way seated into the  piece on the left just like that now  when you do that you'll see you have a  little bit of excess sticking over the  piece on the right and what you're going  to do is you're going to basically pull  the piece down that's in front of you  and you're going to fold this excess  towards you over the right piece just  like that and then make a crease along  the top then you can unfold it now what  you're going to do is the same thing  with the top flap hold this one back and  then fold this one over the right piece  now you'll see you have made two creases  and what you're going to do now is  you're going to open the two flaps on  the right piece now and you're going to  tuck these tips into it just like that  and then what you're going to do is just  close these two flaps on the right now  and just give it a good crease so now  you'll see you will be able to slide  these two pieces within each other  so now you're going to do the same thing  with the piece on the right you're going  to go in a clockwise direction in other  words you're not going to add to the  left you're going to add to the right so  grab another piece hold it this way  rotate it so that this opening here is  vertical just like that slide it into  the piece on the right and put the tip  at the the top here now you can slide it  down here and if it's easier for you  then you could do it like that meaning  it doesn't have to be perfectly lined up  like that but you do want it like that  in the end so if you want to slide it  like that as long as you have it seated  properly meaning as long as this edge is  all the way in it'll be fine  so then do the same thing fold this one  back and take the excess here and fold  it over the piece on the right that  you're adding and make a crease unfold  it then just move away the back piece  and fold the top flap here over the new  piece that you're adding and you're  always folding in towards the center of  these flaps so you're folding this one  like this towards you and this one away  from you then once you've made those  creases you can open the flaps on the  right and you could tuck these tips in  just like that now being that I didn't  tuck them in at the corner here I just  want to slide the new piece all the way  to the end like that and that's  basically how you're going to interlock  them so I'm going to skip ahead to the  seventh piece when you get to the  seventh and eighth pieces you'll notice  that the units will start to overlap but  they're interlocked the same way take  the tip of the seventh piece and slide  it in between the two flaps of the sixth  piece and also make sure that the tip is  also going in between these two flaps  that you previously tucked in you don't  want to slide this underneath there like  that otherwise you'll have problems  sliding it past one another in the end  make sure that it's in between there  just like that  now I've already creased it here but you  guys know what to do so just take the  tips  of the sixth piece and tuck them into  the two flaps of the seventh piece just  like that also and you're going to take  the tip of the first piece here and  you're going to bring it so that it's in  between the two flaps of the seventh  piece now grab the eighth piece and just  open the flaps of the seventh piece a  little bit just like that and you're  going to do the same thing take the two  flaps of the eighth piece now and make  sure that the tip of the first piece  slides into the two flaps there and  you're going to take the tip of the  eighth piece and just kind of push the  whole piece down like that so that the  tip also goes in between the two flaps  of the seven piece just like that okay  so now it should be in there make sure  that the tips are properly in between  the two flaps like this and then all  you're going to do is also interlock  these tips here  so you guys know how to make these  creases fold that back take the back one  fold it towards you now what's a little  bit different is that you already have a  tip in between the two flaps you do not  want to take the tip here and fold it  over the tip nope you want it to be only  over this flap of this of the eighth  piece so you want to take the tip of the  seventh piece and tuck it right in there  okay just like that do the same with the  back flap  so just make sure that you're not going  over that tip like that because if you  do you're not going to be able to slide  this piece out okay that's important so  take that tip and put it on the side  like that you're going to do the same  with the tips of the eighth eighth piece  fold it back and then what you're going  to do you're just going to have to open  these two flaps here on the first piece  and you're going to tuck it in there on  the side open the flap and you're going  to tuck it on side of that tip just like  that so it should look just like that  before you go to transform the ninja  star just double-check that none of the  tips or blades are being covered by any  of these side flap tips then all you  need to do is to grab two opposite  pieces and push them directly towards  each other until the blades have come  out rotate it and do the same thing  until all the blades have been revealed  and there you go you have a transforming  ninja star thanks for watching my  tutorial for the transforming ninja star  if you like the video be sure to click  the thumbs up or like button below and  subscribe by clicking the subscribe  button above also if you leave me a  comment in the comment section I might  feature it in my next video so be sure  to let me know what you guys thought  just one more thing I need to show you  guys how to throw it to throw the  transforming ninja star in the frisbee  or octagon configuration you're going to  want to hold it just like a frisbee but  you're going to angle it like that and  then just want to flick your wrist  outwards I've found with the ninja star  configuration if you throw it like a  frisbee or even if you angle it like  that it's always gonna wind up landing  vertically like this and it will damage  the tips a little bit so I find it the  best just to throw it vertically like  that

